Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.30,0:00:08.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You performed human transmutation?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.30,0:00:10.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've committed that\Nwhich is most sanctioned!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.81,0:00:15.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've had your bodies\Ntaken over to the other side!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.81,0:00:20.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So this is why your title is "Fullmetal"!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.82,0:00:23.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.06,0:02:19.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see, so that's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.35,0:02:27.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's now clear why a kid like you should bear\N the stern-sounding title of "Fullmetal."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.28,0:02:31.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, alchemy forbids \Nthe transmutation of gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.78,0:02:37.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the same time, there is one other inherently forbidden practice,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.54,0:02:38.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that is...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.12,0:02:41.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,human transmutation!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.88,0:02:45.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You miserable, foolish kids!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.04,0:02:49.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You dabbled in human transmutation unaware of its penalties, didn't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.97,0:02:51.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, we didn't! We—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.55,0:02:52.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.64,0:02:57.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just wanted...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.10,0:03:08.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just wanted to see our mom's smiling face one more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.44,0:03:11.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you failed!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.61,0:03:12.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.65,0:03:17.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My brother lost his body,\Nand I lost my left leg and right arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.74,0:03:22.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is what happens when two people try to bring a person back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.75,0:03:26.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, this is what it takes to bring someone back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.63,0:03:30.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you prepared to go through it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.88,0:03:36.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need for concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.97,0:03:41.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have received this\NPhilosopher's Stone from Leto.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.35,0:03:45.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And besides, I am not inexperienced the way they were.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.40,0:03:46.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be ridiculous!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.69,0:03:49.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter what you offer in return,\Nthere are some things that cannot be done!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.94,0:03:52.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then why do you want\Nthe Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.15,0:03:57.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think that if you had this, you could complete your mom's transmutation, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.49,0:03:59.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got it wrong, baldy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.04,0:04:02.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just want to get our original bodies back.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.12,0:04:06.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is, if we {\i1}can{\i0} get them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.46,0:04:12.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll ask you one more time: \Nplease give us the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.13,0:04:17.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,State Alchemist, may the wrath of God befall you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.22,0:04:21.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get down here, third-string,\Nand I'll show you the difference between our levels!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.86,0:04:30.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wretched fools!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.50,0:04:48.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was close!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.13,0:04:51.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.34,0:04:54.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.42,0:04:57.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.97,0:04:58.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This way!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.22,0:05:01.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You fools! There's only one way out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.06,0:05:03.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If there's no way out...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.27,0:05:06.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll just have to make one!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.31,0:05:10.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.73,0:05:16.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After them!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.57,0:05:17.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.66,0:05:20.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That ring...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.53,0:05:22.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are the works of God alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.87,0:05:28.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whether or not one calls it alchemy depends on the person.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.17,0:05:33.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, what they\Ncannot do, I am able to.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.55,0:05:37.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've kept you waiting, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.06,0:05:47.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.23,0:05:50.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cain?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.65,0:05:52.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.28,0:06:02.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cain has had his spirit first resurrected through the works of Leto.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.53,0:06:06.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His body should also become complete in a few days.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.29,0:06:08.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.21,0:06:12.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the work of God, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.18,0:06:24.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If all we wanted to do was\Ntake the Philosopher's Stone,\Nit's not as though we\Ncouldn't have done it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.85,0:06:32.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This evening, a pair of unbelievers sought the minister's life.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.81,0:06:36.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,One of them is short, and the other is wearing ancient armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.79,0:06:39.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.79,0:06:43.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Minister asks that the Faithful refrain from venturing outside
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.43,0:06:42.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}They aren't here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.00,0:06:44.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Hey, go check over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.20,0:06:45.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so as not to suffer any harm.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.96,0:07:00.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No question about it, \Nthat's the guy—the short, stranger kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.76,0:07:03.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you calling an ultra-hyper-pipsqueak?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.72,0:07:05.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never called you that!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.60,0:07:08.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyhow, why don't you just simmer down?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.73,0:07:14.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could you go after\Nthe Minister's life like that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.27,0:07:17.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right! How terrible—a sweet boy like you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.86,0:07:22.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Listen, his miracles are\Nnothing more than alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.74,0:07:24.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By decomposing and restructuring matter—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.78,0:07:25.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a lie!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.83,0:07:33.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Moments ago, my boyfriend, Cain, returned to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.62,0:07:36.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's terrific, Rose!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.75,0:07:39.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After dying in an accident,\NCain has come back to life, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.42,0:07:41.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, you see?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.71,0:07:44.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not just Rose, either!\NThere are many others as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.47,0:07:47.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's right!\NIf that's not a miracle,\Nthen tell me what is!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.64,0:07:50.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Has anyone here actually seen any of those guys?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.64,0:07:52.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone is said to have left town afterwards—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.02,0:07:53.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Silence!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.61,0:07:59.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-The statues of Leto!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.19,0:08:01.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a miracle!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.75,0:08:16.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.53,0:08:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.57,0:08:49.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So this is the proof that\Nyou're a State Alchemist, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.32,0:08:50.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the first time\NI've seen one of these.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.95,0:08:54.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The reason you can transmute\Nwithout a transmutation circle
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.58,0:08:58.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is that this thing works like an amplifier, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.94,0:09:20.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't get any sleep at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.53,0:09:26.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bell's gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.83,0:09:40.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Feed it to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.88,0:09:41.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My hands are like this, and everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.46,0:09:47.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was it really...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.97,0:09:50.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,your boyfriend?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.22,0:10:35.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone is our secret alone,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.64,0:10:36.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.61,0:10:50.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cain... I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.90,0:10:54.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I, um, I just had to talk to you a little...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.33,0:10:57.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.00,0:11:07.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.38,0:11:10.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, I'm terribly sorry about taking the key without permission.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.27,0:11:28.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Rose.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.78,0:11:31.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even with the power of\Nthe Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.28,0:11:33.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it was all I could do to offer up the lives of the birds to God,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.99,0:11:38.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,in an attempt to replace them\Nwith the life of another, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.74,0:11:44.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Perhaps this Chimera, which tweets\Nwith Cain's voice, is not to your liking?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.96,0:11:52.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give my regards to Cain.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.18,0:11:55.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.30,0:11:57.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.94,0:12:09.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is only one other who knows\Nthe secret of the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.12,0:12:20.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's dangerous here. Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.49,0:12:22.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.13,0:12:33.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your flim-flamming is going to be found out soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.34,0:12:37.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Faithful are not likely to distinguish between alchemy and the works of God.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.22,0:12:43.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, in the sense that it brings\Nhappiness to them, they are the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.85,0:12:47.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, what's in it for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.98,0:12:52.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The basic principle of alchemy is equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.07,0:12:57.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're trying to obtain something, you have to pay for it with something of appropriate value.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.57,0:13:00.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People say that\NBrother is a prodigy at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.37,0:13:03.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it's only because he has paid the price of enough effort...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.08,0:13:06.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that Brother is who he is now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.87,0:13:10.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You paid the price, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.25,0:13:13.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An arm, a leg... a whole body...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.30,0:13:17.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and yet now you're\Ntrying to take them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.97,0:13:20.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And your mother...\NWhat happened to her?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.10,0:13:23.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay then,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.10,0:13:24.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess it's time I got started.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.35,0:13:30.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, you're after money, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.01,0:13:31.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.38,0:13:34.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can get all the money I want \Nfrom the donations of the Faithful.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.44,0:13:40.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What I want are believers who would gladly throw their own lives away for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.95,0:13:45.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They believe in resurrection through me\Nand are not afraid to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.04,0:13:49.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In time, they would become an invincible army.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.42,0:13:55.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just you watch, in a few years, \NI will set out to tear this country apart!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.59,0:14:00.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Makes no difference to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.22,0:14:01.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.51,0:14:06.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, you can't really bring anyone back to life, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.72,0:14:08.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course not!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.27,0:14:09.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if I used the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.69,0:14:12.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's no telling what would happen if I performed human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.06,0:14:18.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, for the sake of the Faithful, \Nwho are nothing more than my pawns...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.44,0:14:18.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,would I run the risk of...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.74,0:14:25.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wha—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.08,0:14:27.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\t(1110,1360,\alpha&HFF&)\t(1360,1610,\1a&H00&,\3a&H00&,\4a&B4&)\t(2260,2760,\alpha&HFF&)}What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.12,0:14:32.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long?! How long\Nhas that mic been on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.67,0:14:34.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For the whole time\Nyou've been here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.13,0:14:37.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How... How did you get my broadcast equipment?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.76,0:14:39.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.47,0:14:44.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, what got busted up yesterday was just \Nsome junk that I transmuted to look like him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.39,0:14:46.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! It's all a lie!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.01,0:14:48.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must not believe it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.82,0:15:02.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like I said, I'm on\Na whole different level!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.13,0:15:23.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister, was that broadcast just now for real?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.89,0:15:32.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I do not know what the heretic has broadcast in my voice,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.23,0:15:34.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but it was all a conspiracy!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.40,0:15:38.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As a testament to this, I will eradicate the heretic by the power of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.57,0:15:42.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the power of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.95,0:15:53.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a miracle!\NThe statues of Leto...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.46,0:15:59.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give it up, would you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.46,0:16:06.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Without this, you're limited to transmuting your own Automail, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.34,0:16:10.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pops, I'm about to show you the {\i1}real{\i0} hammer of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.54,0:16:32.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.70,0:16:35.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not even with the Philosopher's Stone could something so gigantic be moved!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.21,0:16:41.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The watch has nothing to do with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.25,0:16:44.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother is the Fullmetal Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.49,0:17:13.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't let you have it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.70,0:17:16.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't let you have the Philosopher's Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.76,0:17:27.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rebound?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.35,0:17:39.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An imitation?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.65,0:17:44.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all the commotion you've raised...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.98,0:17:48.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all the trouble you put me through, it was a fake?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.20,0:17:53.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop jerking me around!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.63,0:18:03.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was quite a wild goose chase, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.84,0:18:07.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I thought we were finally\Ngoing to be able to restore your body.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.55,0:18:10.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You should come first, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.26,0:18:12.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That Automail is so hard on you, and all...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.30,0:18:16.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing more to do\Nbut to keep searching, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.73,0:18:20.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could you do that to us?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.56,0:18:24.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To us, the Minister's miracles gave us hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.82,0:18:28.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we believed, even dead people could come back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.03,0:18:31.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was the only hope we had!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.53,0:18:36.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're saying we should have\Nleft everything the way it was?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.41,0:18:42.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What am I supposed to cling to \Nas I continue living from now on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.42,0:18:44.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.80,0:18:50.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll have to decide that for yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.30,0:18:54.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get up and walk. Move forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.80,0:18:57.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got some fine legs there,\Ndon't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.49,0:19:13.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think Brother did all this for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.37,0:19:15.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He shouldn't have bothered!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.16,0:19:20.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've seen all sorts of things.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.96,0:19:27.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can this be?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.34,0:19:32.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That thing you gave me wasn't the real Philosopher's Stone?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.63,0:19:36.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course not.\NThis city is just a decoy, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.64,0:19:42.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who hear the stories about\Nthe Philosopher's Stone gather here,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.73,0:19:44.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.35,0:19:47.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-Who are you guys? Why are you here?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.07,0:19:51.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust, is it okay \Nif I eat this old man?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.62,0:20:05.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where did that miserable Cornello run away to?\NThat rotten false minister!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.71,0:20:09.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.05,0:20:12.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What went on here?\NThis is awful...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.30,0:20:18.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.90,0:20:30.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a miracle...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.27,0:20:31.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're sure it's not just another trick?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.07,0:20:33.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But they came back to life!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.19,0:20:37.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It seems that the Devil worked wickedness in my absence.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.16,0:20:39.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is everyone all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.74,0:20:44.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're the real...\Nthe real minister, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.87,0:20:49.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cornello-sama!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.13,0:20:51.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were deceived by that kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.21,0:20:52.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.93,0:21:00.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Envy, I'm sorry, but we must ask you to keep that form for a little while.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.85,0:21:12.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've seen all sorts of things.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.32,0:21:14.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to tell you about them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.53,0:21:18.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must not come down the same path as us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.66,0:21:19.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what I believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.29,0:21:32.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were born and raised in a small village east of Central named Resembool.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.21,0:21:35.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's where everything began.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.59,0:21:41.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom!\NMom, look, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.51,0:21:44.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.10,0:21:46.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, my!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.18,0:21:48.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother made it!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.39,0:21:50.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can still only do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.98,0:21:56.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Incredible, both of you!\NYou certainly are his children!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.45,0:22:06.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything\Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.08,0:22:11.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything,\Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.88,0:22:16.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.76,0:22:23.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that\Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.71,0:23:40.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.30,0:23:42.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 3: "Mother..."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.88,0:23:45.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I loved Mom's lullabies.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.01,0:23:50.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom's stew tasted like milk, but Brother loved it.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.56,0:23:52.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why we had to...
